notes:
✓ Domain → the set of all first components (x-values) in a relation.

✓ Range → the set of all second components (y-values) in a relation.

Example:
R = {(−2,1), (−1,0), (0,0), (4,2), (3,5)}

Domain = {−2, −1, 0, 4, 3}
Range = {1, 0, 2, 5}

✓ Quick rule:
Domain → look at the first coordinates.
Range → look at the second coordinates.
